[ledge] Required flat annular head bearings for the two M3×60 cap screws. Their Ø5.8 counterbores surround Ø3.3 through passages and seat at Z268.975, 15.199 mm below the crown. The cap prints crown-down; Tree (auto)/Default support and a driver approach through each open Ø5.8 counterbore before assembly. The full hardware/seat geometry is retained; cleanup and loaded performance remain unqualified.
alternatives: Sloping the bearing removes flat contact under the screw head. A larger through hole loses its seat; moving the seat changes the M3×60 engagement and tip reserve. A closed top obstructs screw and driver access. Keep the flat annular bearing with its open counterbore.
